<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">2 February in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 2 February, from 506 to 2007.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/alaric-ii" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alaric-ii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">506 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,520 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Alaric II issues the Breviary of Alaric</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Visigothic king promulgated a digest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-law">Roman law</a> for the Roman population of his kingdom in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>. It became one of the main channels through which Roman law reached early medieval western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-law">Roman law</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1536">1536 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">490 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pedro de Mendoza founds Buenos Aires</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Spanish expedition founded a settlement on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-de-la-plata">Río de la Plata</a>. Hunger and attacks forced its abandonment in 1541, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-de-garay">Juan de Garay</a> refounded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buenos-aires">Buenos Aires</a> in 1580.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-de-la-plata">Río de la Plata</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1653">1653 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">373 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">New Amsterdam receives municipal government</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> settlement on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manhattan">Manhattan</a> was granted its own city government under Director-General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-stuyvesant">Peter Stuyvesant</a>. The English seized it in 1664 and renamed it <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-amsterdam">New Amsterdam</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1848">1848 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">178 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Treaty of Guadalupe Hidalgo ends the Mexican-American War</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a> ceded about half its territory, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/california">California</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nevada">Nevada</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/utah">Utah</a> and most of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arizona">Arizona</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-mexico">New Mexico</a>, to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> for 15 million dollars, and recognised <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texas">Texas</a> as American.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1943">1943 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">83 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">German Sixth Army's last units surrender at Stalingrad</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The final German forces in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volgograd">Stalingrad</a>'s northern pocket laid down their arms. Some 91,000 were taken prisoner, and the defeat marked a turning point of the war on the Eastern Front.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1971">1971 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">55 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Idi Amin proclaims himself President of Uganda</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A week after his coup, Amin declared himself head of state and suspended parts of the constitution. His rule became one of the most brutal in post-colonial <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> until his overthrow in 1979.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1990">1990 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">36 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">F. W. de Klerk lifts the ban on the ANC</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Opening parliament in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-town">Cape Town</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>'s President legalised the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/african-national-congress">African National Congress</a> and other banned groups and announced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nelson-mandela">Nelson Mandela</a>'s release. Negotiations to end apartheid followed.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/2007">2007 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">19 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">IPCC finds global warming is 'very likely' caused by humans</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Released in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>, the summary of the Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change's fourth assessment called warming 'unequivocal' and very likely due to human emissions. The panel shared that year's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nobel-peace-prize">Nobel Peace Prize</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li></ol>
